    <item>
      <title>N-Body Simulator</title>
      <link>https://fahimfuad.github.io/posts/nbodysimulator/</link>
      <pubDate>Thu, 09 Apr 2026 17:05:03 +0600</pubDate>
      <guid>https://fahimfuad.github.io/posts/nbodysimulator/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h1 id=&#34;n-body-gravitational-simulator&#34;&gt;&#xA;  N-Body Gravitational Simulator&#xA;  &lt;a class=&#34;heading-link&#34; href=&#34;#n-body-gravitational-simulator&#34;&gt;&#xA;    &lt;i class=&#34;fa-solid fa-link&#34; aria-hidden=&#34;true&#34; title=&#34;Link to heading&#34;&gt;&lt;/i&gt;&#xA;    &lt;span class=&#34;sr-only&#34;&gt;Link to heading&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;  &lt;/a&gt;&#xA;&lt;/h1&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;A real-time interactive gravitational N-body simulator built in MATLAB App Designer. Simulates the motion of N celestial bodies under mutual gravitational attraction using Newton&amp;rsquo;s law of gravitation and the Velocity Verlet integration method.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;hr&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;table-of-contents&#34;&gt;&#xA;  Table of Contents&#xA;  &lt;a class=&#34;heading-link&#34; href=&#34;#table-of-contents&#34;&gt;&#xA;    &lt;i class=&#34;fa-solid fa-link&#34; aria-hidden=&#34;true&#34; title=&#34;Link to heading&#34;&gt;&lt;/i&gt;&#xA;    &lt;span class=&#34;sr-only&#34;&gt;Link to heading&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;  &lt;/a&gt;&#xA;&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;#overview&#34; &gt;Overview&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;#features&#34; &gt;Features&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;#physics&#34; &gt;Physics&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;#presets&#34; &gt;Presets&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;#controls&#34; &gt;Controls&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;#export&#34; &gt;Export&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;#known-limitations&#34; &gt;Known Limitations&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;#authors&#34; &gt;Authors&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;hr&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;overview&#34;&gt;&#xA;  Overview&#xA;  &lt;a class=&#34;heading-link&#34; href=&#34;#overview&#34;&gt;&#xA;    &lt;i class=&#34;fa-solid fa-link&#34; aria-hidden=&#34;true&#34; title=&#34;Link to heading&#34;&gt;&lt;/i&gt;&#xA;    &lt;span class=&#34;sr-only&#34;&gt;Link to heading&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;  &lt;/a&gt;&#xA;&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;The N-body problem asks: given N masses in space, each attracting every other through Newtonian gravity, how do they move over time? For two bodies this has an exact analytical solution. For three or more it generally does not — the only way to study it is through numerical simulation.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
